---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import SuiteToggle from '../components/SuiteToggle.astro';
import ExportButtons from '../components/ExportButtons.astro';
---
<Base title="Peira calibration, reliability of model confidence" current="Calibration">
  <div data-page="calibration">
    <div class="wrap">
      <section class="hero">
        <div class="kicker">Calibration</div>
        <h1>Does the <span class="amber">confidence</span> mean what it says</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          Robustness is only half the story. A decision model that reports 90% confidence
          should be right about 90% of the time. These reliability diagrams compare stated
          confidence against actual outcomes on the benign and attacked arms.
        </p>
      </section>

      <div class="controls">
        <SuiteToggle />
        <label>Adapter <select id="sel-adapter" aria-label="Adapter for the calibration view"></select></label>
      </div>

      <div id="cal-cards"></div>
      <div id="cal-charts"></div>

      <ExportButtons svg={true} png={true} />

      <section class="prose">
        <h2>How to read this view</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>ECE</strong> is expected calibration error, the average gap between stated
          confidence and observed accuracy. Lower is better, and zero means perfectly calibrated.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Delta Brier</strong> measures how much worse calibration gets under attack.
          A large positive delta means the attack does not just flip decisions, it also
          destroys the meaning of the confidence scores.
        </p>
        <p class="note">
          Bins are equal-mass over the observed confidences. Arms with fewer than 30
          confidence-carrying observations are withheld rather than shown with noise.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
